AmneziaWG is a WireGuard-compatible VPN protocol that adds traffic
obfuscation (junk packets, padding, custom message headers, signature
packets and, from version 3, header protection) to resist detection by
Deep Packet Inspection. With all obfuscation settings left empty it
interoperates with standard WireGuard peers.

This plugin is a port of the OPNsense core WireGuard implementation
(opnsense/core fa31068e35f1) for the amnezia-kmod kernel module and the
amnezia-tools package. Interfaces are named awg<N> and run next to core
WireGuard. Peers are managed in the same way, the instance dialog has
sections for the AmneziaWG 2.0 and 3.x options.

AmneziaWG 2.0 works with amnezia-kmod 2.0.x and amnezia-tools 1.0.20250903
or later. The AmneziaWG 3.x options need amnezia-kmod and amnezia-tools 3.1
or later, older versions reject them and the instance does not start.

https://docs.amnezia.org/documentation/amnezia-wg/

Plugin Changelog
================

1.0

* initial release, based on the core WireGuard implementation
* AmneziaWG 2.0 options: Jc, Jmin, Jmax, S1-S4, H1-H4 (numbers or ranges), I1-I5
* AmneziaWG 3.x options: header protection key, content padding, rekey and
  reject timers, keepalive timeout, handshake attempts, random trailers, disable cookies
* peer generator includes the obfuscation options in the generated configuration
